# What must never be uploaded.
#
# The deploy only needs dist-web. Everything else is either irrelevant to a
# static host or actively dangerous there: .env holds the service role key and
# the provider key, and supabase/ holds the server code those keys belong to.
#
# Vercel honours .gitignore too, but this file is the one that says so on
# purpose — a change to .gitignore should not be able to silently start
# uploading secrets.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

/supabase/
/scripts/
/src/
/node_modules/
/.expo/
/.git/

*.log
*.tgz
